# Local terraform directories (holds binaries and plugins)
.terraform/

# Distributed state files / backups (contains sensitive architecture data)
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Crash logs
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Override local configuration files
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# Variable files containing actual secret keys/passwords
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json

# Ignore local CLI config files
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# Private spike/evidence artifacts
SPIKE_NOTES.md
*.zip

# NOTE: fixtures/sample-finding-event.json was previously listed here while also
# being tracked, so the ignore had no effect and misdescribed the repo. It is the
# real EventBridge envelope banked by P1, already redacted, and the proposer
# handler tests load it. It is tracked on purpose.

# Internal working docs.
# COST.md and PRODUCTION_GAP.md are deliberately public: they are where deferred
# scope and cost honesty live, and a reviewer has to be able to open them.
#
# docs/ai-workflow.md is the full internal record, including the working rules
# and delivery strategy. AI_WORKFLOW.md is its redacted public counterpart and
# IS tracked. Keep new sessions in both: full detail here, engineering-only there.
PLAN.md
docs/ai-workflow.md

# PLAN-v2.md amends PLAN.md (cuts old R2/R3, adds the operations release). Same
# class of working document, same reason to stay untracked.
PLAN-v2.md

# AI_WORKFLOW.md went private 2026-08-23. It was tracked, so this line only works
# because the same change ran `git rm --cached AI_WORKFLOW.md` (see the fixtures
# note above for the trap). It is now the private running log of AI work; the
# public disclosure of AI use is AI_USAGE.md, drafted from that log.
AI_WORKFLOW.md

# AGENTS.md is the working agreement for AI agents in this repo. CLAUDE.md is its
# one-line import bridge (Claude Code reads CLAUDE.md, not AGENTS.md). Both untracked
# while the agreement stabilizes; intended to become public once it settles.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Superseded plan documents and stale rendered views live here, out of the way
# of agents looking for the current plan (PLAN-v2.md).
docs/archive/

# PLAN.html is a local reading view of PLAN.md, rendered by render-plan.py
# (python3 render-plan.py). It carries the same private content: the account ID,
# the delivery strategy, the drop order. Both stay untracked with their source.
PLAN.html
render-plan.py

# Slice specs and their implementation plans are working documents, like PLAN.md:
# they carry the account ID and the corrections-in-progress against PLAN.md before
# those corrections land. The engineering content reaches the public repo through
# AI_WORKFLOW.md and the ADRs, not through the spec. Listed one file at a time
# rather than by glob, so adding a slice is a deliberate line rather than a
# pattern that silently swallows a doc meant to be published. Each document's
# rendered reading view goes with its source.
docs/p15-boundary-spike-spec.md
docs/p15-boundary-spike-spec.html
docs/p15-implementation-plan.md
docs/p15-implementation-plan.html
docs/p15-consistency-audit.md
docs/p15-consistency-audit.html

# JetBrains / PyCharm
.idea/

# Local env/secrets
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# OS noise
.DS_Store

# Local virtualenvs and tooling
.venv/
.venv-checkov312/
.gstack/
